d42a3b997eec5ab906a8583215c", "encounter_hash": "sha256:5c1312aa6d57c43b50bb82612a880811f2d03cd11f3ed1ea19ae879eb203730e", "archive_hash": "sha256:24a380a0b4c2d19d60de593c2f4dcb295fabfb1556292854a482525af7ce64e2", "public_replay_hash": "sha256:9f5c58596964d1abfec09c3247c6e0b740e83c5c6ff2e88eb9117747afbb7b2d"}, "retrieval_terms": ["a", "a_tem", "active", "all", "an", "and", "are", "asserted", "b0", "b0111_0001", "be", "behavior", "bit", "bits", "by", "cleared", "clk", "clock", "correctly", "de", "design", "does", "edge", "ensure", "every", "following", "functionality", "i", "if", "implement", "implements", "in", "input", "interface", "into", "is", "least", "left", "like", "logic", "lsb", "match", "matches", "matching", "module", "most", "must", "named", "negative", "not", "of", "on", "one", "operate", "otherwise", "output", "pattern", "perform", "ports", "position", "positive", "previous", "recent", "register", "remain", "reset", "retains", "rst_n", "set", "shift", "shifted", "shifts", "should", "significant", "specific", "specified", "synchronously", "that", "the", "this", "to", "topmodule", "unless", "use", "value", "when", "whenever", "with", "would", "you"], "content": {"validation": "public_pass_single_sample_hidden_unknown", "specification_excerpt": "I would like you to implement a module named `TopModule` with the following interface. All input and output ports are one bit unless otherwise specified.\n\n- **Input ports**:\n  - `clk`\n  - `rst_n`\n  - `a`\n\n- **Output ports**:\n  - `match`\n\nThe module should implement an 8-bit shift register that shifts in the input `a` on every positive edge of the clock. The shift register is named `a_tem` and retains the 8 most recent bits of `a`. The module should perform the following functionality:\n\n1. **Reset Behavior**:\n   - When `rst_n` is de-asserted (logic 0), the shift register `a_tem` should be cleared to `8'b0`, and the output `match` should be set to `0`.\n\n2. **Shift Register Behavior**:\n   - On every positive edge of the clock, if `rst_n` is asserted (logic 1), the input `a` should be shifted into the least significant bit (LSB) of the shift register `a_tem`, and the previous bits should shift left by one position.\n\n3. **Matching Logic**:\n   - The output `match` should be asserted (logic 1) whenever the value of ", "applied_patch": "--- a/rtl/sequence.sv\n+++ b/rtl/sequence.sv\n@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@\n \t\t\tbegin \n \t\t\t\tmatch <= 1'b0;\n \t\t\tend\n-\t\telse if (a_tem == 8'b0111_1001)\n+\t\telse if (a_tem == 8'b0111_0001)\n \t\t\tbegin\n \t\t\t\tmatch <= 1'b1;\n \t\t\tend\n", "public_rows": {"W_bug": "visible_pass", "W_preserve": "visible_pass"}, "transfer_summary": {"changed_lines": ["-\t\telse if (a_tem == 8'b0111_1001)", "+\t\telse if (a_tem == 8'b0111_0001)"], "checks_on_transfer": ["Check the current public specification and timing before reusing a previously successful patch."], "scope": "Observed public success only; recheck applicability on a new task."}}}}], "state_hash": "sha256:c5d2924c9fb66f8a1c9ac5618dbe4fa6310a6d454b1feb210ac19a6a7305fc51"}, "losses": [], "gains": [], "incumbent_passed": 4, "candidate_passed": 4, "scheduled_pairs": 4, "incumbent_scores": {"sha256:f8c56ad8df1d5c22e8e6fa95b709f36e698f48c933efe7ba9f708a61b7708185:0": true, "sha256:f8c56ad8df1d5c22e8e6fa95b709f36e698f48c933efe7ba9f708a61b7708185:1": true, "sha256:23471b4b16830f5be400672d2d3e9b3d6e036a47dd5e599c8b8fe13034691dc9:0": true, "sha256:23471b4b16830f5be400672d2d3e9b3d6e036a47dd5e599c8b8fe13034691dc9:1": true}, "candidate_scores": {"sha256:f8c56ad8df1d5c22e8e6fa95b709f36e698f48c933efe7ba9f708a61b7708185:0": true, "sha256:f8c56ad8df1d5c22e8e6fa95b709f36e698f48c933efe7ba9f708a61b7708185:1": true, "sha256:23471b4b16830f5be400672d2d3e9b3d6e036a47dd5e599c8b8fe13034691dc9:0": true, "sha256:23471b4b16830f5be400672d2d3e9b3d6e036a47dd5e599c8b8fe13034691dc9:1": true}, "incumbent_cache_path": "/data2/huangyc/R3E-aic-ic-2026-latest/hard-case-five-round-01/real-all-20261019-052956/Prob001/c